  "body": "in HTMLCanvasElement.getContext, if unsupported context requested, return null. it is defined.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#dom-canvas-getcontext\r\n\r\nbut in OffscreenCanvas.getContext https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#dom-offscreencanvas-getcontext , definition about unsupported context is missing.\r\n\r\ncurrently both of Firefox Nightly and Chrome Stable throws TypeError.\r\n\r\nChrome: `TypeError: Failed to execute 'getContext' on 'OffscreenCanvas': The provided value 'unknown' is not a valid enum value of type OffscreenRenderingContextType.`\r\nFirefox: `TypeError: OffscreenCanvas.getContext: 'unknown' (value of argument 1) is not a valid value for enumeration OffscreenRenderingContextId.`\r\n\r\nIf we respect the current implementation, we should define it to throw a TypeError, but for developers that familiar with HTMLCanvasElement, it expects to return null if request context isn't supported.\r\n",
